{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LadderCosClash","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderCosClash","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CrossingWeightAffine"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderCosClash.cos_correction_ne_affine_even_part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderCosClash.cos_correction_ne_affine_even_part","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCosClash.lean#L89-L99","doc":"**G2 form-clash.** At any gap `α ∈ (0, 2π)` the axiomatised cosine correction\n(even part `cos α < 1`) differs from the even part of the proved affine\ntransport (the constant `1`). Hence the cosine's `O(α²)` content is unsourced\nby the KC19 transport and is carried by the axiom alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderCosClash.cos_lt_one_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderCosClash.cos_lt_one_pos","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCosClash.lean#L79-L87","doc":"`cos α < 1` on `(0, 2π)` — the cosine correction's even part is nonconstant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderCosClash.evalMap_ratio_eq_transportFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderCosClash.evalMap_ratio_eq_transportFactor","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCosClash.lean#L64-L77","doc":"**The KC19 transport IS this affine `T`.** The proved ladder ratio\n`evalMap h z / evalMap h 1` (Möbius in `w`, `evalMap_ratio` at `w₀ = 1`),\nreparametrised by the gap `α = (z−1)h/2`, equals `transportFactor (4/(h(h−2))) α`.\nSo `transportFactor` is not an abstract stand-in — it is the KC19 transport. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderCosClash.transport_odd_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderCosClash.transport_odd_diff","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCosClash.lean#L58-L62","doc":"The affine transport's odd part is `−k·α`: `T(α)−T(−α) = −2·k·α`, nonzero\nexactly when `k·α ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderCosClash.transport_even_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderCosClash.transport_even_sum","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCosClash.lean#L52-L56","doc":"**Even part of the affine transport is the constant `1`.** `T` is affine in\n`α`, so symmetrising `α ↦ −α` cancels the linear term: `T(α)+T(−α) = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LadderCosClash.transportFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderCosClash.transportFactor","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderCosClash.lean#L48-L50","doc":"The affine counit→trace transport factor as a function of the gap `α`, with a\nfixed kernel `k`: `T(α) = 1 − k·α`. Linear in `α`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}